names></name><name><surname>Hiddemann</surname><given-names>W</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>The impact of chemotherapy on Leydig cell function in long term survivors of germ cell tumors</article-title><source>Cancer</source><year>2001</year><volume>91</volume><fpage>1297</fpage><lpage>1303</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Cancer||91|1297||bib13|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">11283930</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib14"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Hansen</surname><given-names>SW</given-names></name><name><surname>Berthelsen</surname><given-names>JG</given-names></name><name><surname>von der Maase</surname><given-names>H</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Long-term fertility and Leydig cell function in patients treated for germ cell cancer with cisplatin, vinblastine, and bleomycin <italic>vs</italic> surveillance</article-title><source>J Clin Oncol</source><year>1990</year><volume>8</volume><fpage>1695</fpage><lpage>1698</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'J Clin Oncol||8|1695||bib14|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">1698935</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib15"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Howell</surname><given-names>SJ</given-names></name><name><surname>Radford</surname><given-names>JA</given-names></name><name><surname>Smets</surname><given-names>EM</given-names></name><name><surname>Shalet</surname><given-names>SM</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Fatigue, sexual function and mood following treatment for haematological malignancy: the impact of mild Leydig cell dysfunction</article-title><source>Br J Cancer</source><year>2000</year><volume>82</volume><fpage>789</fpage><lpage>793</lpage><!--PubMed citation query: 'Br J Cancer||82|789||bib15|'--><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">10732747</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="bib16"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="