g/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="93-6602677f1"/></fig><fig id="fig2"><label>Figure 2</label><caption><p>Effect of hormone levels on quality of life. Mean scores represent the average score for the question. Each question is scored on a 4-point scale from 1 (none) to 4 (very much). Results statistically significant different (<italic>P</italic>&#x02a7d;0.05) from surveillance are indicated by <sup>&#x0002a;</sup>.</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="93-6602677f2"/></fig><fig id="fig3"><label>Figure 3</label><caption><p>Relationship between systolic (<bold>A</bold>) and diastolic (<bold>B</bold>) blood pressure and testosterone status. Lowered refers to a testosterone level below the normal range (see text for details).</p></caption><graphic xmlns:xlink="http://www.w3.org/1999/xlink" mime-subtype="jpeg" xlink:href="93-6602677f3"/></fig><table-wrap id="tbl1" position="float"><label>Table 1</label><caption><p content-type="table-title">Characteristics of patients in long-term follow-up study</p></caption><table frame="hsides" rules="groups" border="1" width="85%"><colgroup><col align="left"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/><col align="center"/></colgroup><thead valign="bottom"><tr><th align="left" valign="top" charoff="50">&#x000a0;</th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>No. of patientsassessed</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Chemotherapy</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Chemotherapy&#x0002f;radiotherapy</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Radiotherapy</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Surveillance</bold></th><th align="center" valign="top" charoff="50"><bold>Total</bold></th></tr></thead><tbody valign="top"><tr><td colspan="7" align="left" valign="top" charoff="50"><italic>Patients in cohort</itali